{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, בְּעֵל","hw":"בְּעֵל","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">בְּעֵל</span></big>  (K<sup>§ 54, 3 γ</sup>) <strong>n. m. owner, lord (</strong>Syriac <span dir=\"rtl\">ܒܥܶܠ</span>, used similarly; cf.BH <a data-ref=\"BDB, בַּ֫עַל\" href=\"/BDB,_בַּ֫עַל\", dir=\"rtl\">בַּ֫עַל</a>, √ <a data-ref=\"BDB, בָּעַל\" href=\"/BDB,_בָּעַל\", dir=\"rtl\">בָּעַל</a>; also 𝔗 <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּעֵיל</span><strong>)</strong>;—cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">בּ׳־טְעֵם</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:8\" href=\"/Ezra.4.8\">Ezr 4:8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:9\" href=\"/Ezra.4.9\">9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:17\" href=\"/Ezra.4.17\">17</a> i.e. <em>commander</em> (Andr<sup>M 56*</sup> as translation of Persian <em>framātār</em>, <em>commander</em>).","next":"BDB Aramaic, בִּקְעָא","prev":"BDB Aramaic, בָּעוּ"}